\section gsALMSolvers_References References

[1] de Borst, R., Crisfield, M. A., Remmers, J. J. C., & Verhoosel, C. V. (2012). Non-Linear Finite Element Analysis of Solids and Structures: Second Edition. In Non-Linear Finite Element Analysis of Solids and Structures: Second Edition. https://doi.org/10.1002/9781118375938

The localize-first singular-point pipeline, the \c swibra emanating-tangent construction,
the fold test function, and several of the design choices in
\ref gsALMSolvers_SingularPoints and \ref gsALMSolvers_BranchSwitching above were checked
against two continuation codes and adopted or adapted from them where noted in the text:

[2] pde2path, algorithm naming per Engelnkemper et al. (2019), Section 2 -- the
bisect-before-classify localization (\c bifdetec), the emanating-tangent construction
(\c swibra), and the arc-length growth control (\c sscontrol) all follow this code's shape.

[3] auto-07p -- the fold test function follows this code's AE toolbox
(\c toolboxae.f90); its inline branch switch (a null-vector nudge, not a true emanating
tangent) is the same family as this library's fallback nudge.

[4] PyNCT -- an independent Python continuation code consulted during the same
review.

\note The design choices above were audited against auto-07p and pde2path, including
divergences that were considered and NOT adopted.

